# Optional. Copy to ~/.config/mcp-qmedia/env (or point MCP_QMEDIA_ENV at it).
# Everything here is non-secret. API keys never go in this file or the repo:
# they live per provider in ~/.config/mcp-qmedia/providers.json (0600, written by
# the web UI), or come from QMEDIA_API_KEY / OPENCODE_API_KEY, or from opencode's
# own store ~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json (entries "opencode-go" / "opencode").

# Default provider override (else the one marked default in the store; built in: go, free)
#QMEDIA_BACKEND=go
# Provider store (0600; may hold keys - keep it outside any repo)
#QMEDIA_STORE=/home/YOU/.config/mcp-qmedia/providers.json
# Where opencode keeps its provider keys
#QMEDIA_AUTH_JSON=/home/YOU/.local/share/opencode/auth.json
# Per-file size cap before ffmpeg transcoding kicks in (bytes)
#QMEDIA_MAX_BYTES=20000000
# HTTP timeout for the model call (seconds) - video can be slow
#QMEDIA_TIMEOUT=300
# Port of the on-demand setup wizard (`mcp-qmedia ui`), 127.0.0.1 only
#QMEDIA_UI_PORT=8938
# Launcher / unit: checkout dir and interpreter (default: .venv/bin/python in the checkout)
#MCP_QMEDIA_DIR=/home/YOU/.local/src/ai-agent-setup/mcp/mcp-qmedia
#MCP_QMEDIA_PYTHON=/home/YOU/.local/src/ai-agent-setup/mcp/mcp-qmedia/.venv/bin/python
